<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shammar Yahrish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 275–310 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shammar Yahrish was a king of Himyar in south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in the late 3rd and early 4th centuries CE. He absorbed the Kingdom of Saba around 275 and conquered the Kingdom of Hadramawt around 300, uniting south Arabia under Himyarite rule for the first time. His inscriptions style him king of Saba, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-raydan">Dhu Raydan</a>, Hadramawt and Yamnat.</p></div>
